 ```
 
+Adding a method that is already supported with the same body support is a no-op.
+Changing the body support of an already supported method - a standard one such as
+`GET`, or one added by a previous `addHttpMethod` call - is rejected with
+`FST_ERR_ROUTE_METHOD_ALREADY_SUPPORTED` unless the `override` option is set:
+
+```js
+// Throws: TRACE is supported without a body
+fastify.addHttpMethod('TRACE', { hasBody: true })
+
+// Allowed: the override is explicit
+fastify.addHttpMethod('TRACE', { hasBody: true, override: true })
+```
+
 > ⚠ Warning:
-> `addHttpMethod` overrides existing methods.
+> Overriding the body support of a standard HTTP method changes the semantics of
+> every route registered for that method, including the routes added by plugins.
 
 #### addSchema
 <a id="add-schema"></a>
